Stellar Swing is a physics game about swinging. You fly a little mining drone with a grappling laser, and it all comes down to when you grab on, when you let go, and how fast you're going when you do.

The Stellar Flame is humanity's last starship, and it's running low on picolinium, the glowing green (and slightly pickle-scented) element that lets it jump between stars. Your job is to swing around five solar systems and collect enough of it to keep the ship going.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*] 45 levels across five solar systems
[*] Open-ended levels with more than one way through, and shortcuts if you're brave
[*] Simple mouse controls: click to grapple, let go to fling yourself off
[*] Spend your picolinium on powerups (jump, jetpack, boost and bullet time) and a slightly silly selection of hats
[*] A story told between each world
[*] Finish the whole game in under an hour to earn the crown
[*] Steam achievements
[*] Original soundtrack by Campbell Logan
[/list]

[h2]A bit of history[/h2]
We made the original Stellar Swing in 2013, after a few of us took a gap year from uni to start a game studio. This is the remaster, with a new look, a proper story and a lot of polish. It's finally finished!
